From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: amlogic: odroid-go-ultra: the headphone jack detect switch

GPIOAO_9 is the headphone jack's detect line (hp_det in Hardkernel's
odroidgoU dts): read on the board 1 with a plug in, 0 without, in GPIO
mode, unused in the mainline dts.

Report it as SW_HEADPHONE_INSERT of an input device "headphones" of its
own, so the event device of the buttons (gpio-keys) stays as it is.
gpio-keys-polled at 20 ms: the meson pinctrl GPIO chip maps no
interrupts (no to_irq), so the interrupt driven gpio-keys cannot use the
line. The contact bounces 1/0/1 within 300 ms as a plug goes in (seen
with a 50 ms debounce-interval), hence 300 ms: gpio-keys-polled reports a
change at the poll that sees it and then skips reading the line for
DIV_ROUND_UP(debounce-interval, poll-interval) = 15 polls, 300 ms; the
next read, 320 ms after the change, reports the settled state (no event
if it is the same). A glitch that a poll happens to see while the plug
stays in still shows as a 0 and, 320 ms later, a 1. No pinctrl state:
the line reads right as it is.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts
@@ -224,6 +224,32 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The headphone jack's detect line (hp_det in Hardkernel's dts): high
+	 * with a plug in. A device of its own after gpio-keys, so the buttons'
+	 * event device stays the same; polled, as the AO GPIO bank has no
+	 * interrupts mapped (gpiod_to_irq() fails on it).
+	 */
+	headphones-detect {
+		compatible = "gpio-keys-polled";
+		label = "headphones";
+		poll-interval = <20>;
+
+		headphones-switch {
+			label = "headphones";
+			linux,input-type = <EV_SW>;
+			linux,code = <SW_HEADPHONE_INSERT>;
+			gpios = <&gpio_ao GPIOAO_9 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			/*
+			 * The contact bounces 1/0/1 within 300 ms as a plug
+			 * goes in. gpio-keys-polled reports a change at once,
+			 * then reads the line again only after
+			 * DIV_ROUND_UP(300, 20) = 15 polls (300 ms).
+			 */
+			debounce-interval = <300>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	memory@0 {
 		device_type = "memory";
 		reg = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0x40000000>;
